   "response_text": "I'll analyze this training run systematically across all artifacts.\n\n## Analysis\n\n### Configuration Review\n- **config.yaml**: Standard MLP setup with 20 epochs, batch size 256, learning rate 0.2 (adam optimizer), no dropout, no weight decay issues (0.0001 is standard)\n- **config.resolved.yaml**: Properly resolved with input_dim=105 and seed=43\n\n### Model Architecture\n- MLP with hidden dims [64, 32], ReLU activation, input_dim=105\n- Single output with BCEWithLogitsLoss (binary classification)\n- No dropout (dropout=0.0)\n\n### Training Metrics Analysis\nLooking at the end-of-epoch metrics:\n- **Epoch 0**: train_loss=0.811, val_acc=0.809 (good initial learning)\n- **Epochs 1-6**: train_loss stabilizes ~0.40, val_acc improves to ~0.847 (peak at epoch 6)\n- **Epochs 7-16**: val_acc remains reasonable (0.817-0.851), some variance\n- **Epochs 17-19**: **DEGRADATION OBSERVED**\n  - Epoch 17: val_loss jumps to 0.621 (was ~0.37-0.41), val_acc=0.841\n  - Epoch 18: val_loss=0.577, val_acc=0.813\n  - Epoch 19: val_loss=0.560, val_acc=0.753 (final, significantly worse)\n\n### Key Observation: Overfitting/Validation Loss Explosion\nThe sharp increase in validation loss (0.37\u21920.621\u21920.560) in the final 3 epochs while training loss remains moderate (~0.45-0.56) is a classic sign of **overfitting or loss of generalization**. The validation accuracy drops noticeably in epoch 19 (0.753, down from 0.847 peak).\n\n### Code Review\n- Training loop is standard and correctly implemented\n- Learning rate is constant at 0.2 (no schedule)\n- No regularization beyond weight_decay=0.0001 (minimal)\n- Dropout is disabled (0.0)\n- No early stopping mechanism\n\n### Hypothesis\nThe model lacks sufficient regularization (dropout is disabled) and the learning rate is not scheduled. After ~6-10 epochs of reasonable learning, the model begins to overfit, evidenced by diverging train/val losses in later epochs. The constant high learning rate (0.2) may prevent convergence to a good solution.\n\n### Diagnosis\nThe run completed successfully (exit code 0), but exhibits a **training instability pattern** \u2014 specifically, overfitting in the later epochs with no regularization mechanisms to prevent it. The disabled dropout and lack of learning rate scheduling are likely causes. This is a **learning_rate_overfitting** or **insufficient_regularization** issue.\n\nThe most direct fix is to enable dropout (which is configured at 0.0) to improve generalization.",
